+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive, dependency-free coffee shop UI. Run `pnpm start` to serve the application.
+
+## Reusable components
+
+- `components.js` exports `icon`, `hydrateIcons`, `button`, `productCard`, `escapeHTML`, and `Modal`.
+- `styles.css` defines shared color, type, radius, and surface tokens, with base, component, and responsive cascade layers. Buttons, filters, product cards, banners, and dialogs can be reused independently.
+- `app.js` holds menu data and connects filtering, product customization, bag quantities, local storage, and preview enrollment.
+
+To render a product card, pass an object containing `id`, `name`, `price`, `badge`, `image`, `alt`, and `description` to `productCard`. Dynamic text is escaped. Use event delegation with `data-product` and `data-add` for card actions.
+
+Create a modal with `new Modal(dialogElement)` and call `open(title, bodyHTML)`. Pass trusted HTML for the body and escape user-supplied text. The native dialog manages focus and Escape dismissal; a bounds-check fallback supports backdrop dismissal in browsers without `closedby`.
+
+The bag persists on the current device. Checkout, member authentication, and live rewards enrollment require a backend. Café addresses and the contact email are illustrative.
+
+## Images
+
+Stock photographs are downloaded from Unsplash and served locally:
+
+- Hero: photo-1442512595331-e89e73853f31
+- Latte: photo-1461023058943-07fcbe16d735
+- Espresso: photo-1510707577719-ae7c14805e3a
+- Cold brew: photo-1517701604599-bb29b565090c
+- Croissants: photo-1555507036-ab1f4038808a
+- Morning buns: photo-1509365465985-25d11c17e812
+
+Source URLs use `https://images.unsplash.com/<image-id>`.
